{"anchor": {"begin": [111, 0, 568.67], "end": [111, 0, 618.67], "env": "lemma", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 49, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "9.7", "source_sha256": "e2cc047bbf1796aa06a93c46137c219eb0c68229be7868cfc386da0cd3f6be9e", "statement": "Lemma 9.7. There exists q big > 0, independent of the correction stage and derivative order, such that every finite partial sum above, before applying summation cutoffs, is well defined on 0 < q < q big . For every fixed stage and output amplitude derivative, its construction and estimate require finitely many input amplitude derivatives. The constants may depend on the correction stage.", "title": null}, "blockers": [], "class": "unspecified", "clauses": [], "correspondence": null, "decls": {}, "findings": [], "heading": null, "id": "P:lemma-9.7", "key": "lemma-9.7", "kind": "lemma", "links": [], "location": null, "mode": "simple", "number": "Lemma 9.7", "paper": "P", "release": "v-ba1f9414ed2f", "schema": "prooflens/manifest@1", "scope": "formal", "scope_note": "", "scope_reviewed": true, "source_evidence": {"pdf_integrity": "unpinned", "placement": "approximate", "state": "pdf-only"}, "source_matches": null, "source_sha256": "e2cc047bbf1796aa06a93c46137c219eb0c68229be7868cfc386da0cd3f6be9e", "statement_tex": null, "status": "not linked", "status_code": "link.none", "suggestions": [], "title": ""}
